<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Natives Land Act, 1913</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1913</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Natives Land Act of 1913 was a law of the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> that barred Africans from buying or renting land outside designated reserves, which then covered about 7 per cent of the country. It ended African sharecropping on white-owned farms in much of the country and drove many families off the land. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sol-plaatje">Sol Plaatje</a> condemned it in Native Life in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> (1916), and the reserves were later enlarged under the Native Trust and Land Act of 1936.</p></div>
